It is a launcher: it signs in to a cluster, starts tools there and draws them as a
flow. It implements none of the methods those tools run, and it grants nothing for
them: each tool keeps its own license and its own notices.

The third-party programs and libraries it uses keep their own licenses; see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Some of them restrict redistribution or hosted use, and those terms reach
this software: it may not be used to give anyone a tool in a way that tool's own license forbids.

